{
  "Makefile": "- File Path: `Makefile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a set of convenient commands (targets) for building, running, stopping, and managing the GoTrade microservices application using Docker Compose.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Variables:\n        - `DOCKER_COMPOSE`: String, module-level, set to `docker-compose`.\n    - Functions / Methods (Targets):\n        - `all`: Public target, default command, calls `up`.\n        - `build`: Public target, builds Docker images for all services.\n        - `up`: Public target, starts all services in detached mode, rebuilding images.\n        - `down`: Public target, stops and removes all services, networks, and volumes.\n        - `restart`: Public target, restarts all services by first calling `down` then `up`.\n        - `logs`: Public target, tails logs from all running services.\n        - `restart-service`: Public target, restarts a specific service identified by the `service` variable.\n        - `test`: Public target, placeholder for running application tests.\n        - `lint`: Public target, placeholder for running code linters.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Uses `.PHONY` to declare targets that are not actual files. Leverages shell commands to interact with `docker-compose`.\n",
  "README.md": "- File Path: `README.md`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a comprehensive introduction to the GoTrade project, detailing its architecture, setup instructions, development commands, and descriptions of its various microservices.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Sections:\n        - `GoTrade - A Golang Microservices Trading Platform`: Project title and brief description.\n        - `Architecture`: High-level overview with a diagram illustrating client, Nginx, backend services, PostgreSQL, and Redis interactions.\n        - `Prerequisites`: Lists required software (Docker, Docker Compose, Go, make).\n        - `Setup \u0026 Running`: Instructions for cloning the repository and using `make up`/`make down` to manage the application.\n        - `Development Commands`: Details various `make` commands for development workflows (build, up, down, restart, logs, restart-service).\n        - `Service Descriptions`: Provides a brief purpose for each core service (`Nginx`, `user-service`, `order-service`, `market-service`, `PostgreSQL`, `Redis`).\n        - `API Documentation`: Mentions future Swagger/OpenAPI integration.\n        - `Environment Variables`: Explains how configuration is managed via environment variables and the use of a `.env` file.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Standard Markdown documentation, includes a high-level architecture diagram, provides clear step-by-step instructions for setup and development.",
  "docker-compose.yml": "- File Path: `docker-compose.yml`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines and configures the multi-container Docker application for the GoTrade platform, including Nginx, user service, PostgreSQL, and Redis.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Services:\n        - `nginx`: Uses `nginx:1.25-alpine` image, maps port 8080 to 80, mounts `nginx/nginx.conf`, depends on `user-service`.\n        - `user-service`: Builds from `./user-service` context, maps port 8081 to 8081, sets environment variables (`APP_PORT`, `POSTGRES_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`), depends on `postgres`.\n        - `postgres`: Uses `postgres:14-alpine` image, sets environment variables for user, password, and database, maps port 5432 to 5432, mounts `postgres-data` volume.\n        - `redis`: Uses `redis:7-alpine` image, maps port 6379 to 6379.\n    - Networks:\n        - `gotrade-net`: A bridge network connecting all services.\n    - Volumes:\n        - `postgres-data`: A named volume for PostgreSQL data persistence.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Standard Docker Compose syntax for service orchestration, including image specification, port mapping, volume mounting, environment variable injection, and service dependencies.\n",
  "nginx/nginx.conf": "- File Path: `nginx/nginx.conf`\n- High-Level Purpose: Configures the Nginx server to act as a reverse proxy and API gateway, routing requests to backend microservices and serving a placeholder for the frontend.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Server Block:\n        - Listens on port 80.\n        - `server_name`: `localhost`.\n    - Location Blocks:\n        - `/`: Handles requests to the root path, currently returns a \"GoTrade Frontend Placeholder\" message.\n        - `/api/user/`: Proxies requests to the `user-service` running at `http://user-service:8081/`, forwarding host, IP, and protocol headers.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Nginx configuration for reverse proxying, API gateway pattern, and static content serving (currently a placeholder).\n",
  "user-service/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `user-service/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines a multi-stage Docker build process to create a minimal and efficient Docker image for the Go `user-service` application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Stages:\n        - `builder`: Uses `golang:1.21-alpine` to download Go modules and build the `user-service` binary with `CGO_ENABLED=0` for a static executable.\n        - Final image: Uses `alpine:latest` as a base, adds `ca-certificates`, copies the pre-built binary from the `builder` stage, exposes port 8081, and defines the command to run the service.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Multi-stage build for smaller image size, static compilation of Go application, minimal base image for production.\n",
  "user-service/go.mod": "- File Path: `user-service/go.mod`\n- High-Level Purpose: Specifies the Go module path and the required Go version for the `user-service` project.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Module:\n        - `gotrade/user-service`: The module path for this Go project.\n    - Go Version:\n        - `1.21`: The minimum Go version required.\n",
  "user-service/main.go": "- File Path: `user-service/main.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the Go `user-service` application, responsible for initializing the HTTP server and defining basic endpoints.\n- Definitions in the File:\n    - Functions / Methods:\n        - `main()`: Public function, the application's entry point. It reads the `APP_PORT` environment variable (defaulting to \"8081\"), registers HTTP handlers for `/health` and `/metrics`, logs the server start, and listens for incoming HTTP requests.\n    - Variables / Constants:\n        - `port`: String, local to `main`, stores the port number the server will listen on, derived from `APP_PORT` environment variable or defaults to \"8081\".\n- Notable Patterns or Logic: Standard Go `net/http` server setup, environment variable-based configuration, basic health check and metrics (placeholder) endpoints.\n"
